        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Warm mist and cool mist add the same moisture to the air. The real differences are a heating element that can scald and costs roughly ten times as much to run, against a cool design that needs a little more attention to water quality and cleaning.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For bedrooms, nurseries and homes with pets, choose cool mist. Choose warm mist only for an adult room where hard water and hygiene of the output matter more to you than the electric bill. Either way, size it to the room, aim for 30 to 50 percent humidity, and keep it clean.
          </p>
        </div>

